WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.170
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:08.910
Neural network-based learning algorithms are
on the rise these days, and even though it

00:00:08.910 --> 00:00:14.710
is common knowledge that they are capable
of image classification, or in other words,

00:00:14.710 --> 00:00:20.039
looking at an image and saying whether it
depicts a dog or a cat, nowadays, they can

00:00:20.039 --> 00:00:22.200
do much, much more.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:27.010
In this series, we covered a stunning paper
that showcased a system that could not only

00:00:27.010 --> 00:00:33.840
classify an image, but write a proper sentence
on what is going on, and could cover even

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:35.570
highly non-trivial cases.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:39.480
You may be surprised, but this thing is not
recent at all.

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.739
This is 4 year old news!

00:00:41.739 --> 00:00:42.770
Insanity.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:48.630
Later, researchers turned this whole problem
around, and performed something that was previously

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.880
thought to be impossible.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.630
They started using these networks to generate
photorealistic images from a written text

00:00:55.630 --> 00:00:56.630
description.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:01.890
We could create new bird species by specifying
that it should have orange legs and a short

00:01:01.890 --> 00:01:03.120
yellow bill.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:09.400
Later, researchers at NVIDIA recognized and
addressed two shortcomings: one was that the

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:15.060
images were not that detailed, and two, even
though we could input text, we couldn’t

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.280
exert too much artistic control over the results.

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.510
In came StyleGAN to the rescue, which was
then able to perform both of these difficult

00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:25.470
tasks really well.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:30.229
These images were progressively grown, which
means that we started out with a coarse image,

00:01:30.229 --> 00:01:34.270
and go over it over and over again, adding
new details.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.200
This is what the results look like and we
can marvel at the fact that none of these

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:40.040
people are real.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.960
However, some of these images were still contaminated
by unwanted artifacts.

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:50.340
Furthermore, there are some features that
are highly localized as we exert control over

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:56.060
these images, you can see how this part of
the teeth and eyes are pinned to a particular

00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:01.659
location and the algorithm just refuses to
let it go, sometimes to the detriment of its

00:02:01.659 --> 00:02:02.899
surroundings.

00:02:02.899 --> 00:02:09.629
This new work is titled StyleGAN2 and it addresses
all of these problems in one go.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:15.329
Perhaps this is the only place on the internet
where we can say that finally, teeth and eyes

00:02:15.329 --> 00:02:20.650
are now allowed to float around freely, and
mean it with a positive sentiment.

00:02:20.650 --> 00:02:25.730
Here you see a few hand-picked examples from
the best ones, and I have to say, these are

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:31.599
eye-poppingly detailed and correct looking
images.

00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:32.849
My goodness!

00:02:32.849 --> 00:02:36.209
The mixing examples you have seen earlier
are also outstanding.

00:02:36.209 --> 00:02:38.909
Way better than the previous version.

00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:44.290
Also, note that as there are plenty of training
images out there for many other things beyond

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:52.549
human faces, it can also generate cars, churches,
horses, and of course, cats.

00:02:52.549 --> 00:02:56.930
Now that the original StyleGAN 1 work has
been out for a while, we have a little more

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:02.909
clarity and understanding as to how it does
what it does, and the redundant parts of architecture

00:03:02.909 --> 00:03:05.540
have been revised and simplified.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:10.969
This clarity comes with additional advantages
beyond faster and higher-quality training

00:03:10.969 --> 00:03:13.040
and image generation.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:18.969
Interestingly, despite the fact that the quality
has improved significantly, images made with

00:03:18.969 --> 00:03:22.290
the new method can be detected more easily.

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.589
Note that the paper does much, much more than
this, so make sure to have a look in the video

00:03:26.589 --> 00:03:27.819
description!

00:03:27.819 --> 00:03:32.089
In this series, we always say that two more
papers down the line, and this technique will

00:03:32.089 --> 00:03:35.110
be leaps and bounds beyond the first iteration.

00:03:35.110 --> 00:03:40.439
Well, here we are, not two, only one more
paper down the line.

00:03:40.439 --> 00:03:42.280
What a time to be alive!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.760
The source code of this project is also available.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.340
What’s more, it even runs in your browser.

